<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01MV">Remark <span data-tag="01MV">6.3.1.18</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets which exhibits $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ as a localization of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ with respect to a collection of edges $W$. Let $[W]$ denote the collection of morphisms in the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ which belong to the image of $W$. Then the induced functor $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{F}: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}$ exhibits the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}$ as a $1$-categorical localization of $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ with respect to $[W]$, in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="01M9" href="/tag/01M9">6.3.0.6</a>. This follows immediately from Example <a data-tag="01ML" href="/tag/01ML">6.3.1.6</a>. </p>
